WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:05.239
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.774
- Hi everyone, 
and welcome to our session

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:12.279
on Core Web Vitals and Search
Engine Optimization, SEO.

00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:15.182
Today, we’ll be talking 
about what SEO is,

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:17.484
how the Core Web Vitals 
play a role there,

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.987
and how you can use Search Console

00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:23.190
to help track and improve
your site's metrics.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:28.195
For many, SEO is a weird
collection of black magic spells,

00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:33.133
but once you dig in a bit
more, it's not at all that.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.168
We've heard that Google is pretty good

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.870
at figuring websites out,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.472
and it's tempting to assume

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:40.340
that having a clean website means

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.145
you don't need to think about
SEO, but it's not that simple.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:49.182
SEO is all about improving
the quality and quantity

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.920
of the traffic a website gets
from normal search results,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.756
so excluding things like ads.

00:00:55.756 --> 00:00:58.692
There are multiple things a
website can do to achieve that.

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:00.727
It differs a bit by search engine,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.863
and I can only speak for Google.

00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:06.900
In general, the main aspects
are the same everywhere though.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.535
Make relevant content.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.471
Users go to search
engines to find out more,

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.440
and your pages might be the resource

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.275
that they're looking for.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.244
This is more than just writing well.

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:18.946
It's also about picking topics

00:01:18.946 --> 00:01:22.182
and phrasing that’s 
used by your audience.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.885
Make the content accessible
to search engines.

00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:27.788
If search engines can't
understand your content,

00:01:27.788 --> 00:01:29.990
it'll be hard for them to recommend it.

00:01:30.891 --> 00:01:32.659
Show why your site is awesome

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.063
using the various signals
that flow into SEO.

00:01:36.063 --> 00:01:38.198
There's a lot that plays in here.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.766
A good way to think about this

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.836
is given there are multiple
good and relevant results,

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.005
how can you show search engines

00:01:45.005 --> 00:01:47.608
that yours is particularly good

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:50.544
and useful answer for users right now?

00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:53.580
The Core Web Vitals flow
into that last group.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.416
For the other aspects of SEO,

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.352
I strongly recommend checking out

00:01:58.352 --> 00:02:00.220
some of the SEO starter guides

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.190
and getting help from experienced SEOs.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.994
It's useful to think of
SEO a bit like usability.

00:02:06.994 --> 00:02:09.396
A little bit of information is helpful

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:10.697
but when it gets serious,

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.800
you want to get the help from experts.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.836
Over to the Core Web Vitals.

00:02:15.836 --> 00:02:18.939
You've heard a lot about the
Core Web Vitals today already.

00:02:18.939 --> 00:02:21.975
So this is really just
a super short overview

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.944
to help get you started.

00:02:23.944 --> 00:02:27.314
The Core Web Vitals
focus on three aspects.

00:02:27.314 --> 00:02:30.717
First, how quickly the page loads;

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:34.354
second, how soon you can
interact with the page;

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.024
and third, how stable the page is

00:02:37.024 --> 00:02:40.994
as it's loading and as the
user is interacting with it.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.497
If you're curious about
more details there,

00:02:43.497 --> 00:02:45.599
be sure to check out the other sessions

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:47.934
and our documentation.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.670
When it comes to data sources,

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:54.675
we differentiate between
field data and lab test data.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:00.347
Field data also called Real
User Metrics or RUM data

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:04.384
is collected from users over
the course of about a month

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:08.588
and is based on what they
experience when viewing your site.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.692
This is a part of the Chrome
User Experience Report,

00:03:11.692 --> 00:03:13.560
in short, CrUX.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.495
Lab tests, on the other hand,

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.299
are generated on demand with
testing tools in your browser

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:23.136
or on a server using settings
that try to approximate

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.272
what users would see.

00:03:25.272 --> 00:03:26.506
For search rankings,

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.774
we use field data

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:32.245
as this is what your site's
users have experienced over time

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:35.182
This makes the data more
representative for your site

00:03:35.182 --> 00:03:38.585
taking into account where
your users are located

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:41.621
and how they access your website.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.557
The Core Web Vitals metrics

00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:47.094
are then combined with
other signals for search.

00:03:47.094 --> 00:03:48.528
We call this combination

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.031
the page experience ranking factor.

00:03:51.865 --> 00:03:54.968
The additional signals
are mobile-friendliness,

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.271
Safe-Browsing, HTTPS security

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:02.809
and compliance with our intrusive
interstitial guidelines.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.811
These have all been around for a while

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.646
and there's much written up about them

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:09.082
so I won't go into much detail here.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.853
We plan to adjust 
these signals over time

00:04:12.853 --> 00:04:16.723
to best reflect a good
user experience for users.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:20.994
We'll give a six months
heads up before any change.

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.764
The data is split by mobile and desktop

00:04:23.764 --> 00:04:27.634
and applied appropriately
for search ranking.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.538
When a mobile page is shown as
a separate AMP URL to users,

00:04:31.538 --> 00:04:33.607
that's what will be used then.

00:04:33.607 --> 00:04:35.976
In other words, if
you're on a mobile page,

00:04:35.976 --> 00:04:39.112
the ranking is only
affected by mobile data

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.314
and the same for desktop.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.583
So in short, for search rankings,

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:47.354
we use a page experience set of metrics.

00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:50.023
These include a few existing signals

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:53.126
as well as the Core Web Vitals.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.261
We track these based

00:04:54.261 --> 00:04:57.264
on what users would 
see separating mobile

00:04:57.264 --> 00:04:59.666
and desktop experiences.

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:02.135
Cool. We looked at page experience,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.336
the Core Web Vitals

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.539
and how they're used in Search.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:08.608
Let's take a look at Search Console now.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:11.611
Search Console is a free
tool for site owners

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:15.315
that gives insights into
Google Search for your website.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.851
Once you've verified ownership

00:05:17.851 --> 00:05:22.022
and given the tool a bit of
time to collect all the metrics,

00:05:22.022 --> 00:05:26.660
it's time to head over to
the Core Web Vitals Report.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.694
In this report,

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:31.198
you'll see graphs for mobile
and desktop showing how

00:05:31.198 --> 00:05:34.935
a relevant sample of
your site's pages score.

00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:36.736
This sample and the scoring

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:40.207
is based on the Chrome user
experience report data.

00:05:40.207 --> 00:05:43.476
That’s the field data 
collected over time.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.578
Because of that,

00:05:44.578 --> 00:05:46.813
any changes that 
you make on your website

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:50.684
will take about a month
to be reflected here.

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:53.320
Clicking through 
to one of these reports,

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.590
you see a graph of the
total number of URLs tracked

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:00.727
and can see the individual
issues flagged below.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.829
Going to one of these issues,

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.465
you'll see a similar graph on top

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.701
together with a list of sample URLs

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:10.670
for its issue type below.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.541
Keep in mind that these reports
are based on the field data,

00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:18.812
so not all of your site's
URLs will be available here.

00:06:18.812 --> 00:06:22.082
It's often useful to focus on
the bigger buckets of issues

00:06:22.082 --> 00:06:26.686
across both the poor and
needs improvement categories.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:30.457
We try to recognize patterns
such as shared templates

00:06:30.457 --> 00:06:32.692
and group those URLs together,

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.594
as fixing the issue once

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.830
can improve large parts of your website,

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.698
which is pretty awesome.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:41.001
A good approach 
to improving these issues

00:06:41.001 --> 00:06:45.438
is to take a bigger issue type
and to work to resolve it.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.274
After recognizing the issue,

00:06:47.274 --> 00:06:49.609
the first step is usually trying

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:54.614
to reproduce the issue locally
or within a testing tool.

00:06:54.648 --> 00:06:56.883
If that’s not possible, 
for bigger issues,

00:06:56.883 --> 00:07:00.353
it's worth narrowing things
down using the various tools

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:02.355
and scripts available elsewhere.

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:05.125
Once you've reproduced the issue,

00:07:05.125 --> 00:07:07.494
you can work to improve the vitals.

00:07:07.494 --> 00:07:09.262
I won't go into details here,

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.798
but be sure to check
out the other sessions

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.033
for more information.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:15.902
As an aside,

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:19.139
sometimes you may notice
that other Google products

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:22.309
or services are slowing down your pages.

00:07:22.309 --> 00:07:24.978
Google Search doesn't
give any special treatment

00:07:24.978 --> 00:07:28.315
to these just like users
generally won't care

00:07:28.315 --> 00:07:31.918
why your pages offer
a bad user experience.

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:33.553
Treat embeds from Google,

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:36.556
just like you would treat
any other embedded resource.

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.859
Once your live website is updated,

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:43.196
you can tell Search Console
that the issue is fixed.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:46.066
This is done in the
appropriate drill-down report

00:07:46.066 --> 00:07:47.167
that we saw before

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:50.603
by clicking the Validate
Fix button on top.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:54.474
Search Console will then start
a review of the URLs flag

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:55.475
and let you know

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:58.078
how your improvements
turned out over time.

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:01.848
Let's get back to SEO.

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:03.516
As mentioned in the beginning,

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:06.953
there's more to SEO than
just page experience.

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:09.589
Some of the factors are listed here.

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.257
When determining the rankings,

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:14.694
we have to weigh these
factors appropriately.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.863
In general, we prioritize pages

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:19.299
with the best information overall,

00:08:19.299 --> 00:08:23.436
even if some aspects of
page experience are subpar.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:24.904
A good page experience

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:28.408
doesn't override having
great relevant content.

00:08:28.408 --> 00:08:29.476
For example,

00:08:29.476 --> 00:08:31.945
if someone is searching
for your company's name,

00:08:31.945 --> 00:08:35.415
it would be expected to
show your company's website,

00:08:35.415 --> 00:08:36.616
even if it's slow

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:40.553
or otherwise provides a
subpar page experience.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.722
In cases where there are multiple pages

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.491
that have similar content,

00:08:44.491 --> 00:08:47.127
page experience becomes
much more important

00:08:47.127 --> 00:08:49.462
for visibility in Search.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:51.064
It's not the only factor.

00:08:51.064 --> 00:08:54.267
And of course there's
much more to a website

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.668
than just Search.

00:08:56.536 --> 00:09:00.206
We found that when a site
provides a good page experience,

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:03.777
it generally performs 
well with users too.

00:09:03.777 --> 00:09:04.778
For example,

00:09:04.778 --> 00:09:08.381
we found users are 24% less likely

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:10.884
to abandon page loads overall.

00:09:10.884 --> 00:09:15.722
In particular, we saw 22%
less abandonment for new sites

00:09:15.722 --> 00:09:19.826
and 24% less abandonment
for shopping sites.

00:09:19.826 --> 00:09:20.960
There are a few changes

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.962
that can show this level of improvement

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:26.232
for online businesses,
and results like these

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:30.136
are part of the reason we
prioritize the web vitals metrics.

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.639
The search ranking change

00:09:32.639 --> 00:09:36.843
is currently planned for
the first half of 2021.

00:09:36.843 --> 00:09:38.311
With this change,

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.413
we're also making all pages eligible

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:43.083
to be featured in 
the top stories carousel

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:47.387
of the search results using
page experience as a guide.

00:09:47.387 --> 00:09:49.022
If you're curious about the details,

00:09:49.022 --> 00:09:52.158
be sure to check out our blog post.

00:09:52.158 --> 00:09:53.726
Well, that was it,

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:54.994
our short excursion

00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:58.498
into the world 
of Core Web Vitals and SEO.

00:09:58.498 --> 00:10:01.267
In short, while there's
more to page experience

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:02.535
than just SEO

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:06.139
and there's more to SEO
than just page experience,

00:10:06.139 --> 00:10:08.508
SEO is also definitely a good reason

00:10:08.508 --> 00:10:11.478
to work on improving your
site's page experience.

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:15.682
I hope you found this session
useful and insightful.

00:10:15.682 --> 00:10:18.485
Don't forget to check out
the other sessions here

00:10:18.485 --> 00:10:23.356
to find out more ways to
improve your website for users.

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:24.357
Bye.

00:10:24.357 --> 00:10:26.893
(upbeat music)

